# Redirect rules, applied by Cloudflare Workers static assets before the asset
# lookup. One rule, and it exists to enforce a single canonical hostname.
#
# The apex is canonical, not `www`. BaseHead emits `<link rel="canonical">`
# pointing at gfqlab.com for every page, and the sitemap only lists the apex.
# Without this redirect the same document would be reachable under both
# hostnames, which splits the canonical signal across two URLs.
#
# It is deliberately NOT in charge of trailing slashes: `html_handling:
# "auto-trailing-slash"` in wrangler.jsonc already owns that, and two layers
# rewriting the same URL is how redirect loops happen.
#
# `:splat` carries the path through, so /work/ecs-aws-infra/ on www lands on
# /work/ecs-aws-infra/ on the apex rather than dropping to the root.
www.gfqlab.com/* https://gfqlab.com/:splat 301